// ── A. Personal Statement ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#v(0.8em)
#text(weight: "bold")[A. Personal Statement]
#v(0.3em)

I first became interested in research during my undergraduate studies in Electrical and Electronic Engineering at the University of Dhaka, where I was introduced to machine learning and its applications in healthcare. I worked under the supervision of Dr. Md Atiqur Rahman Ahad on human activity recognition and participated in international competitions, which strengthened my skills in data analysis and model development. Later, I collaborated with Dr. Muhammad E. H. Chowdhury on a senior-year project focused on physiological signal analysis using deep learning for wearable health monitoring. These experiences sparked my interest in applying artificial intelligence to biomedical problems. Currently, my predoctoral research focuses on generating antibacterial peptides using large language models and narrowing down promising candidates through a deep learning–based screening system. Thirteen peptides were selected for experimental validation against Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria, and three have already shown promising results. Through this work, I am gaining strong interdisciplinary training in computational biology and machine learning. I hope to submit this work as a first-author publication in the coming months, and I am committed to building a long-term career in research focused on AI-driven biomedical discovery.

